# KamerCatch

When finding student housing in the Netherlands became a full-time job, I automated the entire hunt.

## What It Does

KamerCatch runs multiple Playwright-based scrapers every 15 minutes across Dutch rental platforms (Roomspot, Marktplaats, Pararius, Xior, Kamernet), centralizes listings into SQLite, and fires Discord webhook alerts when new affordable rooms appear. A Python script generates personalized email drafts for rapid landlord outreach.

## Technical Highlights

- **Stealth Scraping**: Playwright with user-agent rotation, random execution jitter, and anti-detection configs to avoid IP bans
- **Data Pipeline**: All listings routed through Turso/libSQL into a local SQLite database
- **Real-time Dashboard**: Next.js 14 App Router with live listing feeds
- **AI Agents**: Hermes (Nous Research) + DeepSeek API for boilerplate code generation and Docker debugging
- **Infrastructure**: Docker Compose orchestrates the entire multi-service scraping loop

## What I Learned

This project was a masterclass in tying together disparate technologies into a cohesive system. Web scraping taught me offensive security tactics (beating anti-bot protections), Docker taught me containerization, and the AI agent integration was my first exposure to autonomous coding assistants. Most importantly, it actually solved a real problem — I found housing a month before moving to the Netherlands.

